{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011Wd7K4DzXrkxB5QChjMHSE","type":"tool_result","content":"   187→\n   188→### Phase 0: Preparation\n   189→\n   190→**Step 0.1: Create a feature branch**\n   191→```bash\n   192→git checkout develop\n   193→git pull origin develop\n   194→git checkout -b hrishi/monorepo-migration\n   195→```\n   196→\n   197→**Step 0.2: Verify clean state and establish baseline**\n   198→```bash\n   199→bun run test:unit\n   200→bun run lint\n   201→bun run tc\n   202→git status  # must be clean\n   203→```\n   204→\n   205→Record the baseline results before making any migration changes. This establishes what passes and what fails before the migration, so the implementer can distinguish pre-existing issues from regressions.\n   206→\n   207→**Known pre-existing issues (as of the source snapshot used for planning):**\n   208→\n   209→1. **`bun run tc` (typecheck) fails.** The `tsconfig.json` specifies `\"types\": [\"bun-types\"]`, but the `bun-types` package is stored in `node_modules/.bun/bun-types@<version>/node_modules/bun-types/` rather than directly at `node_modules/bun-types/`. The TypeScript compiler cannot find it via normal module resolution. The newer `@types/bun` package is present and would work, but `tsconfig.json` still references the older package name. This is unrelated to the monorepo migration and should not block it. The implementer should note the failure, confirm it also occurs on a clean `develop` checkout without migration changes, and proceed.\n   210→\n   211→2. **`bun run test:unit` has 9 pre-existing failures.** These are Codex binary locator tests that fail with \"Codex binary not found in node_modules. Ensure @openai/codex-sdk is installed.\" The expected baseline is approximately 1512 pass, 4 skip, 9 fail. These failures are environment-specific (missing Codex SDK binary) and unrelated to the migration. The implementer should confirm the same 9 tests fail on a clean checkout and proceed.\n   212→\n   213→If the implementer encounters additional failures beyond these known ones after making migration changes, those should be investigated as potential regressions. A quick way to check is `git stash && bun run test:unit && git stash pop` to compare before/after.\n   214→\n   215→### Phase 1: Bring docs into the repo\n   216→\n   217→**Step 1.1: Create the `docs/` directory**\n   218→\n   219→Before copying, verify that no `docs/` directory already exists in the repo (e.g., from a prior attempt). If it does, remove it first or abort and investigate. The source snapshot confirms `docs/` does not currently exist in `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`.\n   220→\n   221→Copy the contents of `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` into `docs/` at the runtime repo root. The files to bring in:\n   222→\n   223→```\n   224→app/\n   225→components/\n   226→content/\n   227→public/\n   228→styles/\n   229→bun.lock           (will be removed in step 1.3)\n   230→mdx-components.tsx\n   231→next-env.d.ts\n   232→next.config.mjs\n   233→package.json\n   234→tsconfig.json\n   235→vercel.json\n   236→```\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"774524ca-ef80-4770-b634-d06c9d7eeed4","uuid":"be6d7c42-5db8-4838-b1e6-25f323580111","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"\n### Phase 0: Preparation\n\n**Step 0.1: Create a feature branch**\n```bash\ngit checkout develop\ngit pull origin develop\ngit checkout -b hrishi/monorepo-migration\n```\n\n**Step 0.2: Verify clean state and establish baseline**\n```bash\nbun run test:unit\nbun run lint\nbun run tc\ngit status  # must be clean\n```\n\nRecord the baseline results before making any migration changes. This establishes what passes and what fails before the migration, so the implementer can distinguish pre-existing issues from regressions.\n\n**Known pre-existing issues (as of the source snapshot used for planning):**\n\n1. **`bun run tc` (typecheck) fails.** The `tsconfig.json` specifies `\"types\": [\"bun-types\"]`, but the `bun-types` package is stored in `node_modules/.bun/bun-types@<version>/node_modules/bun-types/` rather than directly at `node_modules/bun-types/`. The TypeScript compiler cannot find it via normal module resolution. The newer `@types/bun` package is present and would work, but `tsconfig.json` still references the older package name. This is unrelated to the monorepo migration and should not block it. The implementer should note the failure, confirm it also occurs on a clean `develop` checkout without migration changes, and proceed.\n\n2. **`bun run test:unit` has 9 pre-existing failures.** These are Codex binary locator tests that fail with \"Codex binary not found in node_modules. Ensure @openai/codex-sdk is installed.\" The expected baseline is approximately 1512 pass, 4 skip, 9 fail. These failures are environment-specific (missing Codex SDK binary) and unrelated to the migration. The implementer should confirm the same 9 tests fail on a clean checkout and proceed.\n\nIf the implementer encounters additional failures beyond these known ones after making migration changes, those should be investigated as potential regressions. A quick way to check is `git stash && bun run test:unit && git stash pop` to compare before/after.\n\n### Phase 1: Bring docs into the repo\n\n**Step 1.1: Create the `docs/` directory**\n\nBefore copying, verify that no `docs/` directory already exists in the repo (e.g., from a prior attempt). If it does, remove it first or abort and investigate. The source snapshot confirms `docs/` does not currently exist in `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`.\n\nCopy the contents of `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` into `docs/` at the runtime repo root. The files to bring in:\n\n```\napp/\ncomponents/\ncontent/\npublic/\nstyles/\nbun.lock           (will be removed in step 1.3)\nmdx-components.tsx\nnext-env.d.ts\nnext.config.mjs\npackage.json\ntsconfig.json\nvercel.json\n```","numLines":50,"startLine":187,"totalLines":922}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T13:36:41.844Z"}
