{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017uvniKjk8ueCQeoCtpNC26","type":"tool_result","content":"   605→### Phase 6: Verify everything works\n   606→\n   607→**Step 6.1: Run the full test suite**\n   608→```bash\n   609→bun run lint\n   610→bun run tc\n   611→bun run test:unit\n   612→bun run test:integration\n   613→```\n   614→\n   615→None of these should be affected by the migration, provided the `tsconfig.json` exclude for `docs/**/*` was added in Step 2.1. Without that exclude, `bun run tc` will fail here. The runtime code is unchanged, test imports use relative paths from `tests/` to `server/`, and Biome's `includes` whitelist only covers runtime files (not `docs/` or `scripts/`).\n   616→\n   617→**Expected pre-existing failures (see Phase 0, Step 0.2 for details):** `bun run tc` will fail due to the `bun-types` resolution issue, and `bun run test:unit` will show approximately 9 pre-existing failures related to Codex binary resolution. These are not regressions — they match the baseline established before migration. The implementer should verify the same tests fail (no new failures introduced) and proceed. If new failures appear beyond the baseline, investigate as potential regressions by stashing changes and re-running.\n   618→\n   619→**Step 6.2: Run schema generation**\n   620→```bash\n   621→bun run generate-schemas\n   622→```\n   623→Verify output exists in both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n   624→\n   625→Note: the unified lockfile may resolve slightly different dependency versions than the previous root-only lockfile (e.g., `typescript` may resolve to a newer patch version). This can cause minor cosmetic changes to schema output (a few lines differing in `schemas/hankweave.schema.json`). In implementation testing, 4 lines changed in the schema file after the migration's `bun install` step. This is a one-time artifact of the dependency resolution change and is expected — include the schema diff in the migration commit. Future `generate-schemas` runs will be stable.\n   626→\n   627→**Step 6.3: Run the runtime build**\n   628→```bash\n   629→bun run build\n   630→```\n   631→Verify `dist/index.js` is created. The build script uses `import.meta.dir` relative paths and `\"./server/index.ts\"` as entry point -- these are all unaffected by the workspace addition.\n   632→\n   633→**Step 6.4: Verify docs build**\n   634→```bash\n   635→cd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n   636→```\n   637→Verify Next.js build succeeds and the `postbuild` Pagefind step runs.\n   638→\n   639→**Step 6.5: Verify npm pack excludes docs**\n   640→```bash\n   641→npm pack --dry-run\n   642→```\n   643→Verify the tarball file list contains only `dist/`, `shims/`, `schemas/`, and metadata files. The `docs/` directory should NOT appear because it's not in the `\"files\"` allowlist.\n   644→\n   645→**Step 6.6: Test the sync dry-run**\n   646→```bash\n   647→bun scripts/test-sync-local.ts --version <current-version> --use-head\n   648→```\n   649→Verify:\n   650→- `docs/` is correctly stripped from the snapshot\n   651→- `\"workspaces\"` is removed from the public `package.json`\n   652→- All existing verification checks pass (the `shouldNotExist` and `shouldExist` lists)\n   653→\n   654→**Step 6.7: Test release dry-run (if on develop with clean tree)**\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"774524ca-ef80-4770-b634-d06c9d7eeed4","uuid":"87838164-6e55-48bf-bfce-c01b13e87969","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"### Phase 6: Verify everything works\n\n**Step 6.1: Run the full test suite**\n```bash\nbun run lint\nbun run tc\nbun run test:unit\nbun run test:integration\n```\n\nNone of these should be affected by the migration, provided the `tsconfig.json` exclude for `docs/**/*` was added in Step 2.1. Without that exclude, `bun run tc` will fail here. The runtime code is unchanged, test imports use relative paths from `tests/` to `server/`, and Biome's `includes` whitelist only covers runtime files (not `docs/` or `scripts/`).\n\n**Expected pre-existing failures (see Phase 0, Step 0.2 for details):** `bun run tc` will fail due to the `bun-types` resolution issue, and `bun run test:unit` will show approximately 9 pre-existing failures related to Codex binary resolution. These are not regressions — they match the baseline established before migration. The implementer should verify the same tests fail (no new failures introduced) and proceed. If new failures appear beyond the baseline, investigate as potential regressions by stashing changes and re-running.\n\n**Step 6.2: Run schema generation**\n```bash\nbun run generate-schemas\n```\nVerify output exists in both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n\nNote: the unified lockfile may resolve slightly different dependency versions than the previous root-only lockfile (e.g., `typescript` may resolve to a newer patch version). This can cause minor cosmetic changes to schema output (a few lines differing in `schemas/hankweave.schema.json`). In implementation testing, 4 lines changed in the schema file after the migration's `bun install` step. This is a one-time artifact of the dependency resolution change and is expected — include the schema diff in the migration commit. Future `generate-schemas` runs will be stable.\n\n**Step 6.3: Run the runtime build**\n```bash\nbun run build\n```\nVerify `dist/index.js` is created. The build script uses `import.meta.dir` relative paths and `\"./server/index.ts\"` as entry point -- these are all unaffected by the workspace addition.\n\n**Step 6.4: Verify docs build**\n```bash\ncd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n```\nVerify Next.js build succeeds and the `postbuild` Pagefind step runs.\n\n**Step 6.5: Verify npm pack excludes docs**\n```bash\nnpm pack --dry-run\n```\nVerify the tarball file list contains only `dist/`, `shims/`, `schemas/`, and metadata files. The `docs/` directory should NOT appear because it's not in the `\"files\"` allowlist.\n\n**Step 6.6: Test the sync dry-run**\n```bash\nbun scripts/test-sync-local.ts --version <current-version> --use-head\n```\nVerify:\n- `docs/` is correctly stripped from the snapshot\n- `\"workspaces\"` is removed from the public `package.json`\n- All existing verification checks pass (the `shouldNotExist` and `shouldExist` lists)\n\n**Step 6.7: Test release dry-run (if on develop with clean tree)**","numLines":50,"startLine":605,"totalLines":922}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T13:36:46.172Z"}
