{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016B9m1dQ1qArsTSzf1TcqVW","type":"tool_result","content":"   710→Migrate to monorepo: bring docs into workspace\n   711→\n   712→- Add docs/ workspace (formerly SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs)\n   713→- Add \"workspaces\" field to root package.json\n   714→- Regenerate bun.lock as unified workspace lockfile\n   715→- Exclude docs/**/* from root tsconfig.json\n   716→- Update generate-schemas.ts to use monorepo-local docs path\n   717→- Add docs/ to strip lists (sync-public.ts, release.ts, test-sync-local.ts)\n   718→- Strip \"workspaces\" from public package.json in transformPackageJson()\n   719→- Update release.ts schema handling for docs/public/schemas/\n   720→- Add --exclude='docs' to test-sync-local.ts rsync\n   721→- Update .gitignore for docs build artifacts\n   722→- Update standard-operating-procedures.md\n   723→- Include minor schema output diff from unified dependency resolution\n   724→```\n   725→\n   726→Note: the migration commit will include a small diff in `schemas/hankweave.schema.json` (a few lines) caused by the unified lockfile resolving slightly different dependency versions. This is expected and cosmetic — see Phase 6, Step 6.2 for details.\n   727→\n   728→Note on merge convention: per SOP Section 4, the repo uses squash merges. When the PR is squash-merged into `develop`, only the PR title becomes the commit message on `develop`. The bullet-point list above is for the feature branch record and the PR body — it will not appear verbatim in `develop`'s git log.\n   729→\n   730→**Step 8.2: Open PR targeting develop**\n   731→\n   732→Follow the existing PR conventions per SOP Section 4:\n   733→- Title: `Monorepo migration: consolidate hankweave-docs into workspace`\n   734→- Body: Problem/approach/files-changed format\n   735→\n   736→**Step 8.3: Optional CHANGELOG entry**\n   737→\n   738→Under `[Unreleased] > Changed`:\n   739→```markdown\n   740→- **Monorepo migration** -- Consolidated documentation site into the development repository as a Bun workspace. No changes to runtime behavior or public-facing interfaces.\n   741→```\n   742→\n   743→This is optional since it's an internal infrastructure change, not user-facing.\n   744→\n   745→**Step 8.4: Archive the old `hankweave-docs` repo (after migration is fully verified)**\n   746→\n   747→This step happens last — after the PR is merged, CI passes on the merged branch, and the Vercel deployment from the monorepo is confirmed working. Do not archive the old repo before these are all green.\n   748→\n   749→1. Archive `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` on GitHub (set to read-only).\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"774524ca-ef80-4770-b634-d06c9d7eeed4","uuid":"edc684c0-cde9-4b6e-9d68-1c866edbda87","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"Migrate to monorepo: bring docs into workspace\n\n- Add docs/ workspace (formerly SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs)\n- Add \"workspaces\" field to root package.json\n- Regenerate bun.lock as unified workspace lockfile\n- Exclude docs/**/* from root tsconfig.json\n- Update generate-schemas.ts to use monorepo-local docs path\n- Add docs/ to strip lists (sync-public.ts, release.ts, test-sync-local.ts)\n- Strip \"workspaces\" from public package.json in transformPackageJson()\n- Update release.ts schema handling for docs/public/schemas/\n- Add --exclude='docs' to test-sync-local.ts rsync\n- Update .gitignore for docs build artifacts\n- Update standard-operating-procedures.md\n- Include minor schema output diff from unified dependency resolution\n```\n\nNote: the migration commit will include a small diff in `schemas/hankweave.schema.json` (a few lines) caused by the unified lockfile resolving slightly different dependency versions. This is expected and cosmetic — see Phase 6, Step 6.2 for details.\n\nNote on merge convention: per SOP Section 4, the repo uses squash merges. When the PR is squash-merged into `develop`, only the PR title becomes the commit message on `develop`. The bullet-point list above is for the feature branch record and the PR body — it will not appear verbatim in `develop`'s git log.\n\n**Step 8.2: Open PR targeting develop**\n\nFollow the existing PR conventions per SOP Section 4:\n- Title: `Monorepo migration: consolidate hankweave-docs into workspace`\n- Body: Problem/approach/files-changed format\n\n**Step 8.3: Optional CHANGELOG entry**\n\nUnder `[Unreleased] > Changed`:\n```markdown\n- **Monorepo migration** -- Consolidated documentation site into the development repository as a Bun workspace. No changes to runtime behavior or public-facing interfaces.\n```\n\nThis is optional since it's an internal infrastructure change, not user-facing.\n\n**Step 8.4: Archive the old `hankweave-docs` repo (after migration is fully verified)**\n\nThis step happens last — after the PR is merged, CI passes on the merged branch, and the Vercel deployment from the monorepo is confirmed working. Do not archive the old repo before these are all green.\n\n1. Archive `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` on GitHub (set to read-only).","numLines":40,"startLine":710,"totalLines":922}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T13:37:03.835Z"}
